  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Before you visit a country, you should learn about its social rules. Because if you don’t, you might find yourself in an "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "awkward",
      "ref": "v-awkward"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " situation. Here are some interesting rules in different countries."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "In Thailand, you can see that the Thai people are almost always smiling. They are very friendly. However, a simple thing can quickly "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "ruin",
      "ref": "v-ruin"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " a Thai person’s mood. In this country, you can’t touch anyone’s head, because Thai people believe that the "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "soul",
      "ref": "v-soul"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " is in the head."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "If you are going to visit "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Chile",
      "zh": "智利"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", remember one simple rule: Don’t eat anything with your hands. In this country, table "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "manners",
      "ref": "v-manners"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " are very important. You should use knives and forks, even when you eat hamburgers and French fries."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "In most parts of the world, people prefer others to be on time for every event. However, "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Mexicans",
      "zh": "墨西哥人"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " think it’s impolite to do so. In Mexico, people are always late for a friend’s party. If they have a business meeting to attend, they won’t be in a hurry. It is considered to be impolite to arrive anywhere on time. This tradition has a very simple explanation. For a very long time, this country had big problems with public transportation. So, being late has become a habit now."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
